== ECON 0100 | Vignette B2 | Supply

=== Q1 | Consumer Surplus

Members of the wizarding world have preferences for pumpkin pasties according to the following demand curve:

$ P_d = 12 - 1/2 Q_d $

Prices are in galleons and quantity is in pasties.

a) Plot and find the area of consumer surplus at a price of $10$ galleons.#blank

b) Plot and find the area of consumer surplus at a price of $5$ galleons.#blank

c) How much did consumer surplus change as the price dropped from $10$ to $5$?#blank

#space

#pagebreak()

=== Q2 | Quantity Supplied

Pumpkin pasties are produced by many sellers according to the following supply curve:

$ P = 2 + 1/2 Q_s $

Prices are in galleons and quantity is in pasties.

a) Find and plot the quantity supplied at a price of $10$ galleons.#blank

b) Find and plot the quantity supplied at a price of $5$ galleons.#blank

c) How much did quantity supplied change as the price dropped from $10$ to $5$?#blank

d) What is marginal cost at $8$ pasties?#blank

#space

